'' See the source's header. The GOLDEN is the assertion: what this defect was about is
'' WHICH SLOT each read names, and no substring says that.
''
'' In the fixed IR the reads written ABOVE a shadowing 'dim' name the outer storage --
'' '@p' rather than '@p$1' in INNER_, '@v' rather than '@v$3', '@s' rather than the
'' static's '@@main$s' -- while every read below one names the inner. The broken
'' compiler sent all of them to the inner slot, which nothing has written yet.
''
'' 'dim as long w = w + 1' is the boundary and is kept deliberately: its initializer
'' reads '@w$5', the variable being declared, because fbc prints 1 for it and not 12.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/shadowing-local-not-visible-above.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' GOLDEN: expected/shadowing-local-not-visible-above.out
